nting on something  then you'll start to stand up they'll  start to know you the next step I would  do is try to identify who the leadership  is at the organization and again the  smaller the company the easier it is to  find out and get in touch with somebody  and try to just set up a time to go and  talk to them people like helping people  who seem motivated and ambitious and  they think  gonna take their advice so as an example  I get asked a lot from local  entrepreneurs and from entrepreneurs on  the web to mentor them and to answer  question for them a lot of times they  just do it through these YouTube videos  the people who are closer in my city of  Toronto I'll often meet up with them but  only the ones who seem really genuine  and who I think are really gonna take my  advice and there's a great feeling of  joy when you feel like you're helping  somebody out and that they're taking  your advice and they're gonna use that  and and there's there's a huge benefit  to mentors as well as mentees in that  mentorship relationship the biggest fear  and the biggest frustration is that  they're not going to do anything with  your advice you're going to waste your  time and then that feels that feels  terrible feels like you just wasted an  hour of whoever long you spent with that  person and so the challenge that you  have is standing out and showing them in  advance and you're the kind of person  who is gonna really listen to advice and  take it and be helpful and not just the  person's gonna waste their time and so  one method that I've used there that  that's been used on me that I found  really helpful was a woman wrote in  saying she's basically just starting up  and she wanted to meet me  to ask my advice on her business and one  of the lines that she used in her email  was something along the lines of even if  it's just walking with you while you're  on your way to a meeting I'll bring the  coffee and treats and I'd be happy to  meet with you for that for that